Package: GPGHS
Type: Package
Title: Spatially Varying Conditional-Dependence Networks with the Gaussian Process Group Horseshoe
Version: 1.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sagnik", "Bhadury", email = "bhadury@upenn.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Jeremy T.", "Gaskins", role = "aut"),
    person("Arvind", "Rao", role = "aut"))
Description: Estimates sparse conditional-dependence networks among p variables
    observed at n locations of a tissue section, with an edge strength that is a
    function of location. The variables can be the expression of genes at the spots
    of a spatial transcriptomics array or the local abundances of cell types in a
    multiplexed image. Each variable is regressed on the others with spatially
    varying coefficients (neighborhood selection); every coefficient function is a
    Hilbert space basis approximation to a Gaussian process with a Matern-3/2
    covariance, and the amplitude of each function has a horseshoe prior with one
    local scale shared by all basis coefficients of the function (the group
    horseshoe of Xu et al. 2016). A predictor is selected when the shrinkage factor
    of its group (Piironen and Vehtari 2017) is below one half, and the two
    directed decisions of a pair are combined by the AND rule. The package also
    provides the preprocessing used in the accompanying article (log-normalization,
    Moran's I screen and Kruskal-Wallis ranking for genes; quadrat counts for cell
    types), a simulator for spatially varying Gaussian graphical models, replication
    summaries between networks, and plotting functions.
